#DESCRIPTION
Magnetic reconnection (Fadeev current-sheet equilibrium) with the HYBRID
solver (solveEM = F, generalized Ohm's law): kinetic ions / fluid electrons,
on a TWO-LEVEL AMR grid backed by a 2D AMReX library (AMReX_SPACEDIM = 2,
built with ./Config.pl -amrex2d -lev=2).  This is the full-PIC AMR
reconnection test (tests/reconnection_amr/PARAM.in) with the field solver
switched to the hybrid path: a thin layer around the central reconnecting
current sheet (|y| < 7.85 d_i) is refined with REFINEREGION to 2x resolution,
so the reconnection zone is resolved at dx = dy = 0.98 d_i while the outer
region stays coarse.  Reconnection plane x-y; details in README.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-31.4                   xMin  [code units; Lx = 2*pi*L*num_islands ~ 62.8 d_i]
 31.4                   xMax
-15.7                   yMin  [code units; Ly = Lx/2 ~ 31.4 d_i]
 15.7                   yMax

#NCELL  (level-0 / base grid)
32                      nCellX
16                      nCellY

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
2                       maxBlockSizeY

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
F                       isPeriodicY

Field boundary conditions on the box faces (periodic in x, outflow/float in y).
#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (x)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
outflow                 fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (y)
outflow                 fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
outflow                 particleBoxBoundaryLo
outflow                 particleBoxBoundaryHi

Hybrid PIC field solver ON (generalized Ohm's law + Faraday RK4).
Full PIC implicit Maxwell/GMRES solve OFF.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Resistive term ON (SI magnetic diffusivity). etaSI = 8.0e5 m^2/s converts to
etaCode ~ 0.001 at uNormSI = 1.0e5.
#RESISTIVITY
8.0e5                   etaResistivity  [m^2/s]

Electron pressure-gradient term ON (isothermal).
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
20.0                    electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Fourth-order hyper-resistivity (grid mode).  The refined level has dx_fine =
0.98 d_i; eta_h is CFL-scaled per level as C_h * dx^4 / dt_sub so both levels
get a stable, consistent diffusion coefficient.
#HYPERRESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaHyperSI      [m^4/s; unused in grid mode]
grid                    etaHyperMode
0.001                   etaHyperCh

#MINIMUMDENSITY
0.0                     rhoMinOhm

Sub-cycle the B update.  The explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale whistler mode.  With dt = 0.02 and the fine-level dx = 0.98 d_i,
nBSubcycle = 4 gives dt_sub = 0.005 (same as the full-PIC dt), safely inside
the RK4 stability region for the compact 2-dx curl stencil.
#BSUBCYCLE
4                       nBSubcycle

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
12.5                    rho [amu/cc]   background ions (n_code ~ nb = 0.2)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
304000.0                T [K]          ion temperature (beta_i ~ 0.5)
0.0                     bx [T]         guide field set by FadeevIC (bg = 0)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Fadeev current-sheet equilibrium initial condition.  The FadeevIC plugin seeds
both nodeB (output mirror) and centerB (live hybrid field) on every AMR level,
and applies the diamagnetic drift velocity kick so the hybrid ions are in
force balance with the pressure gradient.
#TESTCASE
fadeev

FadeevIC sub-parameters.
#FADEEVIC
5.0                     L        (current-sheet half-thickness / d_i)
0.4                     eps      (island size ratio)
2                       numIslands
1.0                     b0       (reference field, code units)
0.0                     bg       (guide-field ratio; 0 = anti-parallel)
-0.05                   perturb  (m=1 seed amplitude)
0.2                     nb       (background/peak density ratio)

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt   (ion-scale; no electron timescale in hybrid)

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
100                     dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
5                       nParticle per cell in X
5                       nParticle per cell in Y

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii planet  plotString   (z cut; degenerate z in true-2D build)
-1                      dn
1.0                     dt
-1                      dx   (multi-level grid requires unstructured point output)

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
20.0                    TimeMax   ~3.2 ion gyroperiods (reconnection develops)

#RUN

AMR setup: a thin box layer around the current sheet (|y| < 7.85 d_i)
is refined (REFINEREGION) to 2x resolution (REFINEMENTRATIO 2); see README.
#REGION
layer                   name
box                     shape
-31.4                   min
 31.4                   max
-7.85                   min
 7.85                   max

#REFINEREGION
0                       iLev
+layer                  regions

#GRIDEFFICIENCY
1.0                     gridEfficiency

#CONSTANTPPV
F                       isPPVconstant   (per-cell particle count; PC static AMR)
